# Append-only files: nearly every pull request adds lines at the same place. A union merge keeps
# the added lines of both sides, so a local `git merge origin/main` does not stop there. GitHub's
# own mergeability check ignores this, and a line added under `## Unreleased` on a branch cut
# before a version was released can land in the released section: check after merging
# (scripts/check-batch.sh prints where the added changelog lines ended up).
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
docs/specifications/TRACEABILITY.md merge=union
docs/specifications/RESERVED.md merge=union
